  "interpretation": {
    "parent": "The existing input-0 SINGLE|ANYONECANPAY signature protects output 0 and admits a changed output 1 in this fixed layout; it does not establish general index pinning.",
    "successor": "Changing only the input parent txid invalidated each of the seven existing Taproot signature modes, including every ANYONECANPAY mode. Their outputs and signature witnesses were held constant.",
    "controls": "All seven original-parent child modes were admitted independently by Core; the DEFAULT child was mined and its fixed recipient and amount checked. This does not claim NONE modes bind payouts.",
    "limitation": "Tests a naive late-data-parent graft onto a presigned successor graph. It does not rule out a different covenant or introspection design and does not authenticate the late data as a valid fork certificate."
